.TH OPENVAS-ENTERPRISE-CONTAINER 1 "2026-07-29" "OpenVAS Enterprise-Container Deployment" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
openvas-enterprise-container \- manage an OpenVAS Enterprise-Container deployment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B openvas-enterprise-container
.I ACTION
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B openvas-enterprise-container
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B openvas-enterprise-container
initializes, configures, updates, starts, stops, and inspects an OpenVAS
Enterprise-Container deployment.  It also manages ingress certificates,
feed synchronization, OCI client credentials, and external OpenVASD scanners.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-init
Initialize the deployment, certificates, and deployment settings.
.TP
.B \-\-init-openvasd
Initialize OCI client certificates for an OpenVASD deployment.
.TP
.B \-\-change-admin-password
Change the gvmd administrator password.
.TP
.B \-\-change-feed-sync-hour
Change the scheduled feed synchronization hour.
.TP
.B \-\-force-feed-sync
Restart feed synchronization immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-update
Download the latest product version.
.TP
.B \-\-run
Start or redeploy the configured deployment.
.TP
.BR \-\-logs " [" \-\-service-name " " NAME "]"
Show deployment logs.  When
.B \-\-service-name
is supplied, show logs for the named service.
.TP
.B \-\-ps
Show deployment status.
.TP
.B \-\-down
Stop the deployment.
.TP
.B \-\-down-volumes
Stop the deployment and remove volumes.
.TP
.B \-\-update-ingress-certs
Replace the ingress TLS certificate and key.
.TP
.B \-\-create-openvasd-certs
Create TLS certificates for an OpenVASD scanner.
.TP
.B \-\-create-openvasd-tar
Create an OpenVASD deployment archive.
.TP
.B \-\-get-openvasds
List OpenVASD scanners registered in gvmd.
.TP
.B \-\-add-openvasd
Register an OpenVASD scanner in gvmd.
.TP
.B \-\-del-openvasd
Remove an OpenVASD scanner from gvmd.
.SH DEPLOYMENT OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-deployment-mode " MODE"
Set the deployment mode.  Valid values are
.B scan
and
.BR openvas .
The default is
.BR ${DEPLOYMENT_MODE} .
.TP
.BI \-\-feed-mode " MODE"
Set the feed mode.  Valid values are
.BR volume ,
.BR service ,
and
.BR mount .
The default is
.BR ${FEED_MODE} .
.TP
.BI \-\-feed-key " FILE"
Use
.I FILE
as the feed key with
.B volume
or
.B service
feed mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-feed-path " PATH"
Use
.I PATH
as the host feed directory with
.B mount
feed mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-feed-sync-hour " HOUR"
Set the scheduled feed synchronization hour.  The valid range is 1 through 24.
The default is
.BR ${GREENBONE_FEED_SYNC_JOB_HOUR} .
.TP
.BI \-\-ccert-mode " MODE"
Set the client certificate mode.  Valid values are
.BR ca ,
.BR cert ,
and
.BR mount .
The default is
.BR ${CCERT_MODE} .
.TP
.BI \-\-ccert-path " PATH"
Use
.I PATH
as the host client certificate directory with
.B mount
client certificate mode.
.SH ADMINISTRATOR OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-admin-password " PASSWORD"
Use
.I PASSWORD
as the administrator password during initialization or a password change.
.SH OCI CLIENT CERTIFICATE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-license-file " FILE"
Read the OCI registry client certificate and private key from the license file
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI \-\-oci-client-cert " FILE"
Use
.I FILE
as the OCI registry client certificate.
.TP
.BI \-\-oci-client-key " FILE"
Use
.I FILE
as the OCI registry client private key.
.TP
.B \-\-init-docker-oci
Install OCI credentials into dockerd using sudo.
.TP
.B \-\-skip-docker-oci
Do not install OCI credentials automatically.  Print the required commands
instead.
.SH INGRESS CERTIFICATE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-ingress-server-cert " FILE"
Use
.I FILE
as the ingress server certificate.
.TP
.BI \-\-ingress-server-key " FILE"
Use
.I FILE
as the ingress server private key.
.SH OPENVASD OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-cn-openvasd " NAME"
Set the OpenVASD common name and scanner hostname to
.IR NAME .
.TP
.BI \-\-openvasd-port " PORT"
Set the OpenVASD scanner port.  The default port is 443.
.TP
.BI \-\-openvasd-uuid " UUID"
Use the scanner UUID returned by
.BR \-\-get-openvasds .
.TP
.B \-\-openvasd-tar-with-images
Include Docker images in the OpenVASD archive.  Disabled by default.
.TP
.B \-\-openvasd-load-images-from-tar
Load packaged Docker images before deployment.  Disabled by default.
.SH HELP OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help message and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Initialize a scan deployment using a Docker volume for feeds
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-init \\
  \-\-oci-client-cert /path/to/product.crt \\
  \-\-oci-client-key /path/to/product.key \\
  \-\-feed-key /path/to/prod-feed.key
.fi
.SS Initialize with a predefined administrator password
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-init \\
  \-\-admin-password 'secure-password' \\
  \-\-oci-client-cert /path/to/product.crt \\
  \-\-oci-client-key /path/to/product.key \\
  \-\-feed-key /path/to/prod-feed.key
.fi
.SS Initialize with scheduled feed synchronization
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-init \\
  \-\-feed-sync-hour 3 \\
  \-\-oci-client-cert /path/to/product.crt \\
  \-\-oci-client-key /path/to/product.key \\
  \-\-feed-key /path/to/prod-feed.key
.fi
.SS Initialize with custom ingress certificates
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-init \\
  \-\-oci-client-cert /path/to/product.crt \\
  \-\-oci-client-key /path/to/product.key \\
  \-\-feed-key /path/to/prod-feed.key \\
  \-\-ingress-server-cert /path/to/ingress.crt \\
  \-\-ingress-server-key /path/to/ingress.key
.fi
.SS Update and start the deployment
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-update
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-run
.fi
.SS Change the gvmd administrator password
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-change-admin-password \-\-admin-password 'new-secure-password'
.fi
.SS Change the scheduled feed synchronization hour
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-change-feed-sync-hour \-\-feed-sync-hour 4
.fi
.SS Restart feed synchronization immediately
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-force-feed-sync
.fi
.SS Show logs and status
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-logs
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-ps
.fi
.SS Stop or restart the deployment
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-down
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-run
.fi
.SS Stop the deployment and remove Docker volumes
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-down-volumes
.fi
.SS Update ingress certificates
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-update-ingress-certs \\
  \-\-ingress-server-cert ./ingress.crt \\
  \-\-ingress-server-key ./ingress.key
.fi
.SS Create OpenVASD certificates
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-create-openvasd-certs \\
  \-\-cn-openvasd sensor.example.com
.fi
.SS Create an OpenVASD deployment archive
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-create-openvasd-tar \\
  \-\-cn-openvasd sensor.example.com \\
  \-\-openvasd-tar-with-images
.fi
.SS Run an extracted OpenVASD archive
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-run \-\-openvasd-load-images-from-tar
.fi
.SS Run an extracted OpenVASD archive on another host port
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-run \\
  \-\-openvasd-load-images-from-tar \\
  \-\-openvasd-port PORT
.fi
.SS Register an OpenVASD scanner
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-add-openvasd \\
  \-\-cn-openvasd sensor.example.com \\
  \-\-openvasd-port 443
.fi
.SS List or remove registered OpenVASD scanners
.nf
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-get-openvasds
.B openvas-enterprise-container \-\-del-openvasd \-\-openvasd-uuid UUID
.fi
.SH SUPPORT
Greenbone support:
.br
https://www.greenbone.net/support/
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR less (1)
